PHP login session in an internal finance tool: the important boundary is clear. Fetch the user by email with a prepared statement, call password_verify(), then session_regenerate_id(true) before storing the user id in the session.

Relevant example:
```text
$statement = $pdo->prepare('SELECT id, password_hash FROM users WHERE email = :email');
$statement->execute(['email' => $email]);
$user = $statement->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
if (!$user || !password_verify($password, $user['password_hash'])) {
    throw new RuntimeException('Invalid credentials');
}
session_regenerate_id(true);
$_SESSION['user_id'] = $user['id'];
```

PHP CSRF protection in a community forum: the important boundary is clear. Generate a random_bytes token in the session, include it in the form, and compare it with hash_equals() on POST before changing state.

Relevant example:
```text
if (!isset($_SESSION['csrf'])) {
    $_SESSION['csrf'] = bin2hex(random_bytes(32));
}
if (!hash_equals($_SESSION['csrf'], $_POST['csrf'] ?? '')) {
    http_response_code(419);
    exit('Invalid CSRF token');
}
```

PHP file upload in a small online shop: the important boundary is clear. Check upload errors, size, MIME type with finfo, and a generated filename; store outside the public directory and never trust the original extension.

Relevant example:
```text
$file = $_FILES['document'] ?? null;
if (!$file || $file['error'] !== UPLOAD_ERR_OK || $file['size'] > 5_000_000) {
    throw new InvalidArgumentException('Invalid upload');
}
$finfo = new finfo(FILEINFO_MIME_TYPE);
if (!in_array($finfo->file($file['tmp_name']), ['application/pdf', 'image/png'], true)) {
    throw new InvalidArgumentException('Unsupported file type');
}
$name = bin2hex(random_bytes(16));
move_uploaded_file($file['tmp_name'], __DIR__ . '/../private_uploads/' . $name);
```

